From 4252743d44bef7fb852ca145bb861ac8e4a47225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:44:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Recover unbound owner-refused submitters without
 mounting a viewer

Check owner availability before worker binding and move submission off the
event loop. An admitted but unbound submission could otherwise outlive an
unavailable owner while the claim remained running. Keep worker-bound exit
recovery, claim identity and ownership checks intact. Retain updater fencing
and do not infer a lost worker solely from missing binding evidence.

Regression coverage exercises owner-unavailable/unbound and bound control paths,
responsiveness during submission, and viewer resume behavior. Performance and
natural live recovery remain separate acceptance gates.

